Stabwound wrote:
> I believe that my main problem is overpreparing for Gehennom. I don't think
> I've ever stepped foot past the VoTD without at least -30AC. I'm starting to
> think that is overkill. What would be a safe minimum AC to tackle Gehennom
> and beyond?

30,000 turns is a fairly quick "normal" ascension, IMO.  40-50,000 is
probably about average.  <20,000 is in the "speed ascension" range.

My first ascension of the tournament I was at AC -7 (and maybe 120hp)
through Orcustown.  If you have some outs, there is no real cutoff
point; I was just running around mapping stairs and gathering whatever
scrolls and armor I found until I god somewhere I felt uncomfortable;
having the Eye, I was then able to airlift out.  It postponed any ?EA
festival or alchemy until I had more resources to work with (giving me
longer to find pieces of the AK before I started writing ?EA).

> Also, how do people generally handle stashes? I find myself making an early
> stash, and then having to move my entire stash down to around the level
> before Medusa, which obviously takes a lot of time if I can't find a way to
> levelport.

I almost always levelport.  Also don't be a complete pack
run/exhaustive searcher, I run through Gehennom these days (buy
clairvoyance in the Valley and then dive through as quick as possible,
digging past Orcus and similar) .  The only exception is if I'm short
resources (not enough potions/scrolls) in which case I'll map some
levels by hand on the way up.

> Do people generally 'j'ump everywhere? I've noticed a few players on NAO
> jumping a lot, which saves a lot of turns. I've actually never really
> considered jumping boots, but they look pretty damn handy on Astral.

If you're trying to set speed records (as opposed to just ascending
reasonably quickly) jumping boots are almost mandatory.  Most people
don't jump everywhere, though, except for Rast and the other
record-setters.

On astral, OTOH, I view jumping boots as almost mandatory.  Really if
you have intrinsic speed then jumping boots are a better option through
everywhere but Gehennom, IMO.



